    {
      "id": "phase3-0035",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 110,
      "y": 455,
      "width": 820,
      "height": 220,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 595,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1015,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1761490000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 17,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "text": "CORE REALITIES\n• Partial failure: one dependency can fail while others work.\n• A timeout does not prove the remote operation did not happen.\n• Retries need bounds, backoff, jitter, and idempotency.\n• CAP trade-off matters during a network partition.\n• Strong consistency favors fresh/ordered reads; eventual consistency allows temporary staleness.\nASK: Is stale data acceptable? Can a retry duplicate a side effect?",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "CORE REALITIES\n• Partial failure: one dependency can fail while others work.\n• A timeout does not prove the remote operation did not happen.\n• Retries need bounds, backoff, jitter, and idempotency.\n• CAP trade-off matters during a network partition.\n• Strong consistency favors fresh/ordered reads; eventual consistency allows temporary staleness.\nASK: Is stale data acceptable? Can a retry duplicate a side effect?",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
