      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 17,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "text": "CONSISTENT HASHING\n• Hash keys and nodes onto a logical ring; assign a key to the next node according to the ring rule.\n• Adding/removing a node typically remaps only a portion of keys.\n• Virtual nodes improve balance and support heterogeneous capacity.\n• Useful for distributed caches and partition placement.\n• Does NOT automatically provide replication, durability, consensus, or hot-key protection.\nCOMPARE: hash(key) % N can remap many keys when N changes.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "CONSISTENT HASHING\n• Hash keys and nodes onto a logical ring; assign a key to the next node according to the ring rule.\n• Adding/removing a node typically remaps only a portion of keys.\n• Virtual nodes improve balance and support heterogeneous capacity.\n• Useful for distributed caches and partition placement.\n• Does NOT automatically provide replication, durability, consensus, or hot-key protection.\nCOMPARE: hash(key) % N can remap many keys when N changes.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
